# Vite dev env (committed — nothing here is secret; use .env.local for machine-local overrides).

# "Sign in with Google": the OAuth client ID from Google Cloud Console (a PUBLIC identifier —
# the GIS ID-token flow uses no client secret anywhere). Unset → the Google button hides.
#
# To get one: https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials →
# Create Credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application. Add BOTH
#   http://localhost  and  http://localhost:3000
# to "Authorized JavaScript origins" (no redirect URIs needed for this flow), and configure
# the OAuth consent screen (branding) once for the project. Use the SAME value as the
# backend's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.
# TODO(bt,2026-07-21): TEMPORARY client ID borrowed from another project — replace with a
# fresh OAuth client created for this product's real domain before launch.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=788843034237-b1314stpq8h74ntlo3jivdusudik9ged.apps.googleusercontent.com
